add("Mommit-1x4krb3", None, "parent_unspecified", "toddler_12_24_months", "trigger_moment", ["sleep_consultant", "night_wakings", "pacifier"], "We have scheduled a consult with a sleep specialist but it’s a month away and I’m starting to feel desperate.", "18-month-old has never slept through; wakings worsened after the pacifier was stopped cold turkey.")
add("Mommit-1x4krb3", None, "parent_unspecified", "toddler_12_24_months", "failure_story", ["gentle_method", "pacifier"], "We did a gentle sleep training before cutting the paci, I successfully transitioned away from going to sleep in my bed to in his own toddler bed with just my hand on his belly. That all went right out the window when we took the paci.", "Gains from gentle training lost at pacifier weaning.")
add("Mommit-1x4krb3", "pgel9ap", "parent_unspecified", "toddler_12_24_months", "pain", ["night_wakings", "maternal_exhaustion"], "I’m not sure I can keep this up for years ha", "Reply while waiting for the specialist appointment.")
add("toddlers-1x4n2an", None, "parent_unspecified", "toddler_12_24_months", "objection", ["app_tracking", "subscription_resentment", "price_value"], "And I don’t want an expensive membership like Nanit! lol.", "Toddler moving to a bed; parent shopping for a room camera.")
add("toddlers-1x4n2an", "pgrfjn2", "parent_unspecified", "toddler_12_24_months", "price_signal", ["app_tracking", "subscription_resentment", "price_value"], "Nanit is so expensive. I can’t come to the idea of paying another 120$ membership per year for an already expensive camera….", "Rejecting a camera brand's yearly subscription on top of the hardware price.")
add("NewParents-1x4no2l", "pgf8rpu", "new_mother", "baby_2_4_months", "purchase", ["sleepwear", "price_value"], "They are a no name brand. I bought them for the same day delivery in a bout of exhaustion this morning because its randomly chilly this week and baby was cold.", "First-time mum doubting a pack of thick sleep sacks bought online for a 3-month-old.")
add("NewParents-1x4no2l", "pgf9hrz", "new_mother", "baby_2_4_months", "purchase", ["sleepwear", "price_value"], "I saw the recommendations for Woolino and was going to see about buying one secondhand. I bought these this morning on a whim.", "Premium sleep sack wanted but only affordable second-hand.")
add("sleeptrain-1x4r1ub", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "failure_story", ["course_purchase", "night_wakings"], "5.5mo, day 15 of TCB (no pop-ins), still 60 min bedtime protests and 80+ min MOTN wakes. Schedule inside, what are we doing wrong?", "Post title; course plan followed in detail, with a cold and rolling interrupting.")
add("sleeptrain-1x4r1ub", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "pain", ["course_purchase", "guilt", "cry_it_out"], "Thanks. We're tired and we feel terrible to hear him cry still so much after 14+ nights.", "Closing line after a minute-by-minute log.")
add("sleeptrain-1x4r1ub", "pggktlk", "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "tried_failed", ["course_purchase", "night_weaning", "consistency_failure"], "I follow the guidelines that say that I shouldn’t go in if he’s crying but last night I caved in after 2 hours of crying at that time…", "Asking whether to wean the second night feed.")
add("sleeptrain-1x4w7t2", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "failure_story", ["course_purchase", "ferber", "consistency_failure"], "We did a version of Ferber (taking Cara babies) around 5 months, with high hopes since our oldest took to it really well. He struggled with it a lot more, with 45+ minutes of scream-crying at bedtime and regular night wakes even several weeks into sleep training.", "8-month-old second child; parents have since gone back to rocking.")
add("sleeptrain-1x4w7t2", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "fear", ["sleep_props", "consistency_failure"], "I worry it’s created a monster though, since at this point he goes right to scream crying when he wakes, and won’t calm down for anything other than being held.", "After abandoning timed check-ins.")
add("sleeptrain-1x4w7t2", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "others_said", ["partner_disagreement", "cry_it_out", "gentle_method"], "Husband is pushing for CIO, and while I kinda hate that idea, idk if a gentler method would work at this point.", "Waking 3-6 times a night and up at 5:30; a toddler is woken too.")
add("beyondthebump-1x552qz", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "failure_story", ["sleep_consultant", "gentle_method", "short_naps"], "Yesterday I rocked her to sleep without any crying, and she still only slept about 30 minutes in her crib. So the short naps happen either way.", "Consultant-suggested drowsy-but-awake practice with a 7-month-old ended in sobbing.")
add("beyondthebump-1x552qz", "pgjdv4l", "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "objection", ["sleep_consultant", "gentle_method", "personalization"], "But even with that support, she became really upset, which is why I’m questioning whether this approach is a good fit right now. I’m going to discuss a smaller, more gradual step with the consultant.", "Parent stayed by the crib and picked her up each time.")
add("sleeptrain-1x55uj8", "pgk0fnh", "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "question", ["sleep_consultant", "information_overload"], "How can I shift this earlier, and what should I tackle first—wake-up time, naps, bedtime, or independent sleep—without cutting too much sleep after rough nights?", "Same parent, cross-posted; consultant's target wake windows not being met.")
add("sleeptrain-1x5fhps", None, "new_mother", "regression_4_months", "tried_failed", ["book_purchase", "regression_4_month", "cry_it_out"], "In desperation and deprivation I’m plowing through Precious little sleep and trying the “fuss it out” method. However, baby never fussed. She fussed for one minute and straight into the big cries. This first time mom lasted 5 minutes before soothing and rocking to sleep.", "Nearly 5 months; regression started at 3.5 months and never ended.")
add("sleeptrain-1x5fhps", None, "new_mother", "regression_4_months", "fear", ["sleep_training_values", "guilt"], "Is crying actually okay or am I teaching her I’m not coming to save you? Overwhelmed, over thinking and tired.", "Doubts before committing to a method.")
add("sleeptrain-1x5foxq", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "success_story", ["course_purchase", "night_wakings"], "His sleep drastically improved after just a few nights (going from \\~8 wakeups to just one) but he's still crying a lot when we put him down", "Week 3 of a paid course method with a 9.5-month-old.")
add("sleeptrain-1x5foxq", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "pain", ["course_purchase", "short_naps", "cry_it_out"], "Part of me wants to throw in the towel altogether (I can't deal with the crying anymore!)", "Night wakes down to one; naps not yet tackled.")
add("sleeptrain-1x61oof", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "failure_story", ["sleep_consultant", "night_weaning", "chair_method"], "We hired a sleep consultant to help drop the night feeds and help make bedtimes a bit smoother and things went disastrously.", "9-month-old; check-ins on night one, chair method on night two.")
add("sleeptrain-1x61oof", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "regret", ["sleep_consultant", "money_back", "guilt"], "The next morning I quit the sleep training program. She had cried so hard she had lost her voice and I had completely lost my nerve..", "Quit the paid consultant program after two nights.")
add("sleeptrain-1x61oof", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "regret", ["sleep_consultant", "short_naps", "cosleeping"], "Things are so much worse after attempting sleep training. I know I didn’t stick with it long enough but her poor squeaky voice broke me.", "Naps now 30-40 minutes; baby in the parents' bed every night since.")
add("sleeptrain-1x61oof", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "pain", ["guilt"], "Do I just give up and wait out whatever developmental regression this is? Is this just my life now? I think I broke my baby.", "Post titled with 'mom failure'.")
add("beyondthebumpUK-1x62noy", None, "parent_unspecified", "regression_4_months", "trigger_moment", ["sleep_consultant", "free_advice", "short_naps"], "Has anyone worked with a sleep consultant that they would recommend? I’ve tried the advice on the sleep train subreddit but doesn’t seem to be working for my 4.5 month old", "Free subreddit advice failed; parent now looking to pay.")
add("beyondthebumpUK-1x62noy", "pgrpe6u", "parent_unspecified", "regression_4_months", "pain", ["short_naps"], "The 28 min naps are killing me! When did it get better?", "Reply in the consultant-recommendation thread.")
add("beyondthebumpUK-1x6fqgn", None, "parent_unspecified", "unknown", "others_said", ["transition_to_cot", "price_value", "cosleeping"], "A friend recently told me that practically nobody they know uses their cotbed all the way through for their toddler/preschooler, and that most people end up switching to floor beds, double beds, or co-sleeping anyway.", "Weighing whether a cotbed is worth the extra money.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7f8sz", None, "parent_unspecified", "regression_4_months", "failure_story", ["course_purchase", "ferber", "regression_4_month"], "Night 2 of taking Cara babies and I feel like it’s been worse than before we started.", "4-month-old was waking every 90 minutes; parents chose shorter check-ins than the course.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7f8sz", None, "parent_unspecified", "regression_4_months", "pain", ["course_purchase", "cry_it_out"], "She basically cried off and on last night from 10:52-1:52 and it was the most traumatizing thing for me.", "Followed by a minute-by-minute timer log of both nights.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7f8sz", "ph3ll0h", "parent_unspecified", "regression_4_months", "belief", ["sleep_training_values", "dream_feed"], "Ugh idk I’m all over the place. I was against this all but was so desperate for sleep.", "Unsure whether to keep the course's dream feeds.")
add("NewParents-1x7fbyb", "ph3osrd", "parent_unspecified", "regression_4_months", "others_said", ["sleep_training_values", "maternal_exhaustion"], "I’m aware how old my child is thank you! We were approved by our pedetrician as well. I can’t be a parent when I’m running in 1 hour of broken sleep each nigh but thanks for your input.", "Cross-post; replying to commenters who said 4 months is too young.")
add("NewParents-1x7fbyb", "ph3teat", "parent_unspecified", "regression_4_months", "objection", ["course_purchase", "ferber", "personalization"], "I meant we don’t want to go to 15! 10 is already too  \nMuch.", "Parents shortening the course's check-in intervals.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7s3lr", None, "experienced_mother", "toddler_12_24_months", "belief", ["course_purchase", "wake_windows", "comparison_other_babies", "personalization"], "I think I can finally admit that my first daughter was “high sleep needs” and so taking Cara babies wake windows worked very well for her… compared to my second who has been struggling for months.", "13-month-old second daughter at daycare three days a week with split nights.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7s3lr", None, "experienced_mother", "toddler_12_24_months", "belief", ["course_purchase", "wake_windows", "nap_transition"], "I’ve never gone over 5 hours for the afternoon wake window. I think because that’s what TCB recommends and it worked for my first daughter.", "Course chart followed for the second child despite months of split nights.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7s3lr", "ph6tq81", "experienced_mother", "toddler_12_24_months", "others_said", ["course_purchase", "daycare_naps"], "Lol what’s funny is that TCB email support suggested going back to the two naps.", "Course's email support versus commenters' one-nap advice.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7s3lr", "pha9e6m", "experienced_mother", "toddler_12_24_months", "success_story", ["wake_windows", "free_advice", "nap_transition"], "She slept through the night! 12 hours of wake time and last ww being 5 hours.", "After commenters' advice to stretch wake windows beyond the course chart.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7v29i", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "pain", ["app_tracking", "ferber"], "The issue is our current monitor alerts me for everything. Every time he rolls over or fusses for literally two seconds my phone buzzes.", "Day 4 of training a 5-month-old; parent shopping for a smart monitor.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7v29i", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "question", ["app_tracking", "price_value"], "Does cry detection help with timing check-ins or am I overcomplicating this?", "Post title: overwhelmed by monitor options.")
